  "label": "Racist Stereotype: White People Smell Like Bologna",
  "description": "A derogatory racial stereotype that dehumanizes white people by associating them with the smell of bologna, a processed meat product. This stereotype is used to mock and demean white individuals based on their race, implying they are unclean, unpleasant, or inferior. It is a form of racialized body odor mockery, which is a common trope in racist humor and hate speech.",
